# EASY GAS — cron schedule EXAMPLE (Phase 10F artifact)
# =====================================================
#
# SAFE ARTIFACT: template only. It runs nothing until an operator installs it.
# Replace <DEPLOY_DIR>, <DEPLOY_USER> and the log/backup paths with real
# absolute values. Prefer EXTERNAL cron over any in-process timer — an
# in-process timer would run once per PM2 worker (docs/PRODUCTION-RUNTIME-10C.md).
#
# Install as a dedicated file so it runs as the deploy user, e.g.:
#     sudo cp deploy/crontab.example /etc/cron.d/easygas
#     sudo chown root:root /etc/cron.d/easygas && sudo chmod 644 /etc/cron.d/easygas
# (In /etc/cron.d the 6th field is the USER to run as — shown below. If instead
#  you use `crontab -e` as the deploy user, DELETE the <DEPLOY_USER> column.)
#
# NOTES that apply to every job:
#   * All maintenance CLIs default to DRY-RUN; "--apply" is what actually acts.
#   * Each job appends to its own log; rotate these with logrotate.
#   * `cd <DEPLOY_DIR>` first so .env / knexfile / node_modules resolve.
#   * Secrets come from the environment / the app's .env — never inline here.
#   * Stagger the times so nightly jobs don't contend for DB/IO.

# Ensure a sane PATH for node/npm (adjust to your Node install; nvm users must
# point at the concrete version dir, cron does not source your shell profile).
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
SHELL=/bin/bash

# --- 1. Nightly retention cleanup (03:30) -----------------------------------
# Deletes expired/revoked sessions, expired OTP rows and terminal SMS-outbox
# rows past retention; recovers stale SMS PROCESSING leases. Bounded batches,
# idempotent, guarded by a MySQL advisory lock (concurrent runs no-op).
30 3 * * * <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && npm run cleanup -- --apply >> /var/log/easygas/cleanup.log 2>&1

# --- 2. Daily audit hash-chain verification (02:15) -------------------------
# Verifies the tamper-evident audit log hash chain. Read-only; alert on
# non-zero exit (a broken chain means tampering or corruption — investigate).
# NOTE: `audit:verify` is being added by another Phase 10F contributor. Confirm
# the exact npm script name once merged; adjust here if it differs.
15 2 * * * <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && npm run audit:verify >> /var/log/easygas/audit-verify.log 2>&1

# --- 3. Weekly deep evidence reconcile (Sun 04:10) --------------------------
# Reconciles the evidence DB records against object storage. --deep does the
# thorough (more expensive) pass; --apply performs the audited fixes. Run
# weekly off-peak. Drop --apply first if you want to review a dry-run.
10 4 * * 0 <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && npm run reconcile -- --deep --apply >> /var/log/easygas/reconcile.log 2>&1

# --- 4. Nightly MySQL backup (01:00) ----------------------------------------
# Calls the Phase 10F backup script (server/scripts/backup-mysql.sh). It reads
# DB_* and BACKUP_DIR from the environment, never echoes the password, and
# writes a timestamped gzip dump. IMPORTANT: take the DB backup and the
# evidence backup (job 5) as a CONSISTENT PAIR — schedule them close together
# and treat them as one recovery point.
0 1 * * * <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/easygas/mysql bash scripts/backup-mysql.sh >> /var/log/easygas/backup-mysql.log 2>&1

# --- 5. Nightly evidence backup / off-site sync (01:20) ---------------------
# Replicates the PRIVATE evidence bucket to an off-site, versioned bucket.
# APPLY=1 makes it actually sync (default is dry-run). Uses the AWS profile /
# environment for credentials — never embeds them. Runs shortly after the DB
# backup so the pair stays close in time.
20 1 * * * <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && APPLY=1 EVIDENCE_SRC=s3://<SET_IN_ENV_src_bucket> EVIDENCE_DEST=s3://<SET_IN_ENV_offsite_bucket> bash scripts/backup-evidence.sh >> /var/log/easygas/backup-evidence.log 2>&1

# --- (optional) Active risk-policy sanity check (06:00) ---------------------
# Prints/validates the active risk policy. Uncomment to alert if none is active.
# 0 6 * * * <DEPLOY_USER> cd <DEPLOY_DIR> && npm run risk-policy >> /var/log/easygas/risk-policy.log 2>&1

# A trailing newline is required by cron:
